# Component Rules

## Component Structure

### 1. Basic Rules
- **One component per file**: Each component in its own file
- **File naming**: PascalCase for component files (e.g., `ProductCard.js`)
- **Component naming**: Match file name exactly
- **Barrel exports**: Use `index.js` files for clean imports
- **Co-location**: Keep related components in feature folders
- **Client directive**: Add `'use client'` only when needed (interactivity, hooks, browser APIs)

### 2. Uniform Component Structure
Every component MUST follow this exact structure for consistency:

```javascript
/**
 * Component description
 * @param {Object} props
 * @param {type} props.propName - Prop description
 * @param {string} props.variant - Component variant (optional)
 * @param {boolean} props.disabled - Disabled state (optional)
 * @param {Function} props.onClick - Click handler (optional)
 * @param {React.ReactNode} props.children - Component content
 */
'use client'; // Only if needed (interactivity, hooks, browser APIs)

import React from 'react';
import styled from 'styled-components';
import { theme } from '@/styles/theme';

const StyledComponentName = styled.element`
  /* Base styles - mobile-first */
  padding: ${props => props.theme.spacing.md};
  color: ${props => props.theme.colors.text.primary};
  background-color: ${props => props.theme.colors.background.primary};
  border-radius: ${props => props.theme.borderRadius.md};
  transition: all ${props => props.theme.transition.duration} ${props => props.theme.transition.timing};
  
  /* Responsive - enhance for larger screens */
  @media (min-width: ${props => props.theme.breakpoints.sm}) {
    padding: ${props => props.theme.spacing.lg};
  }
  
  @media (min-width: ${props => props.theme.breakpoints.md}) {
    padding: ${props => props.theme.spacing.xl};
  }
  
  /* Variants */
  ${props => props.variant === 'primary' && `
    background-color: ${props.theme.colors.primary};
    color: ${props.theme.colors.text.onPrimary};
  `}
  
  ${props => props.variant === 'secondary' && `
    background-color: ${props.theme.colors.secondary};
    color: ${props.theme.colors.text.onSecondary};
  `}
  
  /* States */
  &:hover {
    opacity: 0.9;
    transform: translateY(-2px);
  }
  
  &:focus {
    outline: 2px solid ${props => props.theme.colors.primary};
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }
  
  &:active {
    transform: translateY(0);
  }
  
  &:disabled {
    opacity: 0.5;
    cursor: not-allowed;
    pointer-events: none;
  }
`;

export const ComponentName = React.memo(({ 
  variant = 'default', 
  disabled = false, 
  onClick, 
  children, 
  ...props 
}) => {
  return (
    <StyledComponentName
      variant={variant}
      disabled={disabled}
      onClick={onClick}
      aria-label={props['aria-label']}
      {...props}
    >
      {children}
    </StyledComponentName>
  );
});

ComponentName.displayName = 'ComponentName';
```

### 3. Theming Requirements
- **Always use theme**: Never hardcode colors, spacing, typography, or breakpoints
- **Theme access**: Access theme via `props.theme` in styled components
- **Dark/light mode**: Components must work with both themes automatically
- **Theme variables**: Use theme variables for:
  - Colors: `props.theme.colors.*`
  - Spacing: `props.theme.spacing.*`
  - Typography: `props.theme.typography.*`
  - Breakpoints: `props.theme.breakpoints.*`
  - Border radius: `props.theme.borderRadius.*`
  - Transitions: `props.theme.transition.*`
  - Shadows: `props.theme.shadows.*`

### 4. Responsive Design Requirements
- **Mobile-first**: Always write mobile styles first, then enhance for larger screens
- **Breakpoints**: Use theme breakpoints consistently:
  ```javascript
  @media (min-width: ${props => props.theme.breakpoints.sm}) { /* 768px */ }
  @media (min-width: ${props => props.theme.breakpoints.md}) { /* 1024px */ }
  @media (min-width: ${props => props.theme.breakpoints.lg}) { /* 1440px */ }
  ```
- **Fluid typography**: Use relative units (rem, em) for typography
- **Flexible layouts**: Use CSS Grid and Flexbox for responsive layouts
- **Touch targets**: Minimum 44x44px for interactive elements on mobile
- **Container queries**: Use container queries when appropriate for component-level responsiveness

### 5. Performance & Efficiency
- **React.memo**: Use `React.memo` for components that don't need frequent re-renders:
  ```javascript
  export const ComponentName = React.memo(({ ...props }) => {
    // Component code
  });
  ComponentName.displayName = 'ComponentName';
  ```
- **Layout components**: Always wrap Header, Footer, and Navigation with `React.memo`
- **Code splitting**: Use `next/dynamic` for heavy components:
  ```javascript
  const HeavyComponent = dynamic(
    () => import('@/components/HeavyComponent').then(mod => ({ default: mod.HeavyComponent })),
    { 
      loading: () => <div>Loading...</div>,
      ssr: false 
    }
  );
  ```
- **Minimal dependencies**: Import only what you need, use tree shaking
- **Avoid inline styles**: Prefer styled-components over inline styles
- **Optimize images**: Always use `next/image` for images

### 6. Reusability & Customization
- **Composition over configuration**: Prefer composition over complex configuration
- **Props for variants**: Use props for component variants (primary, secondary, etc.)
- **Default props**: Provide sensible defaults for all props
- **Extend components**: Extend existing styled components when possible:
  ```javascript
  const StyledExtendedButton = styled(StyledButton)`
    /* Additional styles */
  `;
  ```
- **Generic components**: Create generic, configurable components that can be reused
- **Single responsibility**: Each component should have one clear purpose
- **DRY principle**: Never duplicate code - extract to reusable components

### 7. Component Organization
- **Layout components**: Place in `components/layout/`
- **UI components**: Place in `components/ui/`
- **Feature components**: Place in `components/features/[feature-name]/`
- **Common components**: Place in `components/common/`
- **Barrel exports**: Use `index.js` files for clean imports

### 8. Accessibility Requirements
- **Semantic HTML**: Use semantic HTML elements (button, nav, main, etc.)
- **ARIA labels**: Provide ARIA labels for interactive elements without visible text
- **ARIA roles**: Use ARIA roles when needed
- **ARIA states**: Indicate element states (disabled, expanded, etc.)
- **Keyboard navigation**: Ensure all interactive elements are keyboard accessible
- **Focus management**: Include visible focus states for keyboard navigation
- **Color contrast**: Ensure sufficient color contrast (use theme colors)
- **Alt text**: Provide alt text for images

### 9. Modern Patterns
- **ES6+ features**: Use modern JavaScript (arrow functions, destructuring, template literals)
- **Hooks**: Extract reusable logic into custom hooks
- **Async/await**: Use async/await for async operations
- **Error boundaries**: Use error boundaries for component error handling
- **Type safety**: Document props with JSDoc comments for better IDE support

### 10. Component Best Practices Checklist
Every component must:
- [ ] Follow the uniform component structure
- [ ] Use theme variables (no hardcoded values)
- [ ] Be fully responsive (mobile-first approach)
- [ ] Include JSDoc documentation for all props
- [ ] Use `React.memo` when appropriate
- [ ] Include accessibility features (ARIA, semantic HTML, keyboard navigation)
- [ ] Have proper error handling
- [ ] Use barrel exports
- [ ] Follow naming conventions
- [ ] Be lightweight and efficient
- [ ] Support customization through props
- [ ] Be reusable and composable
